---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import ToolPage from "@bt/ui/ToolPage.astro";
import AdSlot from "@bt/ui/AdSlot.astro";
import SalarioLiquidoCalc from "../../components/SalarioLiquidoCalc.tsx";
---
<Layout
  bleed
  lang="en"
  title="Brazil net salary calculator 2026 (CLT) | Baitaan"
  description="Work out your 2026 net salary in Brazil with the INSS and income tax tables and the new income tax exemption up to R$ 5,000 (Law 15.270/2025). Free, no sign-up."
>
  <ToolPage
    heading="Net salary calculator 2026 (Brazil)"
    lead="Since January 2026, people earning up to R$ 5,000 a month pay no income tax at source in Brazil. The INSS social security deduction still applies, from 7.5% to 14% by bracket."
    updated="Updated: November 2026"
    sourcesHeading="Sources"
    sources={[
      { href: "https://www.planalto.gov.br/ccivil_03/_ato2023-2026/2025/lei/L15270.htm", label: "Law 15.270/2025 (income tax reduction)" },
      { href: "https://www.gov.br/inss/", label: "INSS: 2026 contribution table" },
    ]}
  >
    <SalarioLiquidoCalc client:load lang="en" />

    <Fragment slot="guide">
      <h2>How to calculate net salary</h2>
      <p>Net salary = gross salary − INSS − income tax − other deductions. INSS is calculated bracket by bracket. Income tax is calculated on gross pay minus INSS and dependents (or the simplified deduction of R$ 607.20, whichever is higher).</p>

      <h2>2026 examples</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>R$ 5,000: INSS R$ 501.51, no income tax, net R$ 4,498.49.</li>
        <li>R$ 6,000: INSS R$ 641.51, income tax R$ 385.10 after the reduction, net R$ 4,973.39.</li>
      </ul>

      <AdSlot slot="0000000000" label="Advertisement" />

      <h2>Earning between R$ 5,000 and R$ 7,350</h2>
      <p>In this range the tax isn't zero, but it is lower. The reduction is R$ 978.62 minus 13.3145% of the salary. Above R$ 7,350 the normal table applies.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </ToolPage>
</Layout>
